<title>ITALY: Mediolanum 1996 life premiums up 25 pct.</title>
<headline>Mediolanum 1996 life premiums up 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian insurance and financial services group Mediolanum SpA said on Wednesday that 1996 life insurance premium income rose 25 percent from 1995 to more than 1.18 trillion lire.</p>
<p>The company, jointly owned by Silvio Berlusconi's Fininvest SpA and group managing director Ennio Doris, said in a statement the size of the increase was well above the market average.</p>
<p>Group investment fund gross income rose 29 percent in 1996 due mainly to good performances by money market and bond funds, it said, but did not give a figure.</p>
<p>Mediolanum shares closed on the Milan stock exchange 1.96 percent up at 14,303 lire.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
